{title: A Voice in the Wilderness}
{subtitle: John 1:19–36; Matthew 3:1–6; John 3:27–30}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 118}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×16

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Out in the wilderness of Judea in the burning heat of day
A man in camel's hair was calling and he would not walk away
Locusts and wild honey and a leather belt of hide
All Jerusalem came out to him down by the Jordan's side
Re[B]pent, for the kingdom of heaven [D#m]has come near
And they went [B]down in the river with their [C#]sins confessed and clear
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am [D#m]a voice crying [C#]out in the wil[G#m]derness
[D#m]Make straight the [F#]way of the Lord
[C#]Make straight the [G#m]way of the Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The priests came from the city asking who he claimed to be
Not the Christ and not Elijah, not the one they came to see
I baptize with water
Among you stands one you do not know
The one who comes after me
Whose sandal strap I am not worthy to untie
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am a voice cry[C#]ing out in the [G#]wilderness
[D#m]Make straight the [F#]way of the Lord
[C#]Make straight the [G#]way of the Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]The next day he saw Jesus coming toward him
[B]Look, the Lamb of God
Who [C#]takes away the sin of the [D#m]world
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am a voice cry[C#]ing out in the [G#]wilderness
[D#m]Make straight the [F#]way of the Lord
[C#]Make straight the [G#]way of the Lord [D#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He must increase
I must decrease
He must increase; I must decrease
{end_of_verse}
